// ============================================================================
// Resolution · PARAM FLOW — interprocedural (invocation linking). Type a method's
// PARAMETER receiver by the CONCRETE types callers actually pass at that argument
// position, instead of the declared parameter type.
//
// `void write(IVersionedSerializer s, ...) { s.serialize(...) }` — the declared param
// type IVersionedSerializer fans s.serialize() to every serializer. But if callers pass
// `write(FooSerializer.serializer, ...)`, then at that boundary `s` is FooSerializer.
// Link each resolved call's ARGUMENT expr type to the callee's parameter at the same
// position, then type PARAMETER-reference receivers from it.
//
// COMPOSES WITH THE CAP, like local-flow: purely POSITIVE additions to expr_type (the
// concrete type resolves the call directly; the residual declared-interface fan is
// dropped by dispatch-cap's !cha_wide_base). No negation → stratifies (param_flow_type
// <- expr_resolves_to_method + expr_type(arg); expr_type(recv) <- param_flow_type: one
// positive mutual-recursion SCC).
//
// Uses expr_call_candidate (the SOUND, pre-overload candidate set) NOT expr_resolves_to_method:
// the disambiguated relation is computed with overload-pruning NEGATIONS (expr_pruned / dominated
// / win_*), and reading it here would drag those negations into the expr_type <-> candidate cycle
// (non-stratifiable). expr_call_candidate is positive, so param_flow_type stays in the positive
// SCC (like local_flow). Cost: an arg links to the params of ALL name/arity candidates at the site
// (a sound over-approx across overloads) — extra types are harmless (concrete ones resolve, the
// residual fan is capped).
//
// java_expression (25): 1 edgeRole 6 parentExpressionHash 7 position 10 literalValue(name)
//   14 referencedEntityKind 24 uniqueHash
// java_method_parameter (13): 0 name  1 position  2 method  12 hash
// ============================================================================

// concrete type flowing into callee's parameter at position `pos` (from a candidate call's
// ARGUMENT at that position).
//
// ONLY A TYPE THE PARAMETER CAN HOLD. The candidates at a site are every overload of the name, so
// an argument's type also flowed into the overloads it cannot be passed to: in
// `fromJson(JsonElement json, Type t) { return fromJson(json, TypeToken.get(t)); }` the String,
// Reader and JsonElement arguments of the sibling overloads' recursive calls all flowed into each
// other's `json`, every overload's parameter then held all of them, and the overload choice -- which
// reads exactly that type -- found a contradiction at every candidate and kept them all. A flowed
// type is kept where it is the declared type, a subtype of it, or the declared type is Object or
// unresolved (a type variable, an unstaged type with no external node): narrowing, never widening.
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_resolves(_, param, _, d), t = d.
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_resolves(_, param, _, d), type_ancestor(t, d).
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_resolves(_, param, _, d), param_is_object(d).
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_external(param, x), t = x.
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_external(param, x), type_ancestor(t, x).
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), param_decl_untyped(param).
// A class EXTENDING an unstaged class (an exception over an unstaged IOException, a stream over an
// unstaged FilterInputStream) may reach an unstaged or library declared type through superclasses no
// IR shows, so it is kept against one; never against String, which is final. Implementing an
// unstaged interface is not enough: a builder that is a CharSequence is no StringBuffer.
.decl param_flow_ext_super(t:symbol)
param_flow_ext_super(t) :- java_type_reference(_, "SUPER_TYPE", t, _, _, _, _, "0", _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, ref),
    type_ref_external(ref, _).
param_flow_ext_super(t) :- type_ancestor(t, a), param_flow_ext_super(a).
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_external(param, x),
    param_flow_ext_super(t), !string_type_id(x).
param_flow_type(param, t) :- param_flow_in(param, t), method_param_type_resolves(_, param, _, d),
    type_prov(d, "lib"), param_flow_ext_super(t), !string_type_id(d).
.decl param_flow_in(param:symbol, t:symbol)
param_flow_in(param, t) :-
    applicable_candidate(call, callee),
    java_expression(_, "ARGUMENT", _, _, _, _, call, pos, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, argE),
    expr_type(_, argE, t),
    java_method_parameter(_, pos, callee, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, param).
.decl param_decl_typed(param:symbol)
param_decl_typed(param) :- method_param_type_resolves(_, param, _, _).
param_decl_typed(param) :- method_param_type_external(param, _).
.decl param_decl_untyped(param:symbol)
param_decl_untyped(param) :- java_method_parameter(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, param), !param_decl_typed(param).

// PARAMETER receiver reference takes the flow-in type(s) (positive; cap drops residual fan).
expr_type("client", recv, t) :-
    java_expression(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, name, _, _, _, "PARAMETER", _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, recv),
    expr_ultimate_method("client", recv, m),
    java_method_parameter(name, _, m, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, param),
    param_flow_type(param, t).
